# Architecture Split

Loremetry is a **Vue + Rust/Axum** web app: **Rust owns behavior**, **Vue owns presentation**.

## Rust (`crates/core`, `crates/web`)

- Analysis, DB, documents, market APIs, HTTP/SSE
- Business rules (what counts as a chapter, validation)
- Prefer new Axum routes / invoke bridge commands over doing work in the UI

## Vue (`ui/`)

- Layout, forms, panels, styling, user interaction
- Call the backend via `invoke` from `ui/src/api.ts` / composables; render results
- Do **not** reimplement parsing or analysis in the frontend

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — Vue inventing story structure
await mkdir(`${parent}/${name}/Manuscript`)

// ✅ GOOD — Vue collects input, Rust does the work
await invoke('init_story', { request: { name } })
```
